With no noise the two sit in a periodic orbit and neither wins.  From
one ray per five million instructions down to one per two hundred
thousand, the flatter and slower lineage wins, and at the bottom of that
window the faster one goes extinct in every seed.  Below 200,000 the
comparison stops being about the innovation: lineages persist as clouds
of damaged creatures, and the cost per cell of the survivors says so.
